WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.840
Kotoko-chan, can you please
call Onii-chan down?

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.060
Okay!

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.730
It’s been a while since I’ve did this.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:15.740
I was wondering what would happen at one point,
but now I can be with Irie-kun again.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.410
Irie-kun, your mom asked you to come downstairs for tea.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.000
I’m busy right now.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.080
What are you doing?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.970
This is... a medical book?

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.600
Why are you looking at something like this?

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.130
Oh, be quiet! I’m studying, okay?

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:40.180
Eh? You? Why?

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.520
Because I’m going to transfer to the Medical Department.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.650
Oh, to the Medical Department?

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.940
What?! Irie-kun!

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.760
You’re gonna become a doctor?!

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.210
Only if I pass.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.820
Don’t tell my parents yet.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.190
Sure. I understand.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.450
You have my support.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.070
No thanks.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.950
Nothing good ever comes from your support.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.100
But, isn’t there anything...?

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.180
How about a shoulder massage?

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.590
That’s enough! Get out!

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.700
What was that about? Sheesh!

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.820
Eh? But...

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.520
Could it be that I’m the only person who knows about this?

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.780
Irie-kun, are you done with the procedures?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.880
It’s so amazing that you passed with just one try.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.510
Obviously. I actually studied this time.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:06.220
So, you’re really going to become a doctor.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.720
Which would mean...

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:11.360
Doctor, I’ve brought the charts.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.900
Perhaps I should ask you to get some ointment to apply on my love too.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.960
Just kidding.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.330
Hey, you were having another wild fantasy there, weren’t you?

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.540
Eh? Of course not.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:27.590
Nevermind that. Anyways, spring break starts tomorrow, right?

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:31.280
All the transfer procedures are done.
So, let’s go on a trip somewhere and party.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.500
I’ve already made plans.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.420
What plans?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.790
Not telling.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.030
Aww, no way...

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.510
See you.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.400
Wait!

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.650
Aihara-kun.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:56.310
Sudou-sempai, you <i>do</i> know what plans Irie made, don’t you?

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.910
Of course!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.570
He’ll be spending his break working.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.950
Huh? Work? Where?

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:07.530
Some anmitsu would sure be nice for dessert.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.900
Fine...

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:15.350
Excellent.This top secret information is for your ears only.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:17.890
Actually...

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.790
Romance Village?!

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.670
Okay, I’m going to shoot.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:40.730
Okay!

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:41.860
Okay, say cheese.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.230
Cheese!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.170
Irie-kun!

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:47.700
We came.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.120
Onii-chan!

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.310
I was having a bad feeling about today.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:55.630
Yuuki, only you? What about Mom and Dad?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.030
Papa can’t get leave from work.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:02.130
And Mama said that she couldn’t possibly leave Papa alone in the house.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.840
Your mother really, really regrets not being able to come.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.970
I can imagine.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.740
Oh, you’re here, Aihara-kun.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.480
Sudou-san, you’ve really done it, haven’t you?

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.460
What are you talking about?

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.220
I sure hope you didn’t tell anyone else.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:23.510
Irie-kun! Good afternoon!

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.610
Matsumoto Yuuko!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:30.320
Oh, Matsumoto! Welcome!

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.420
And who might this wonderful young lady be?

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.230
My little sister.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:39.800
I’m Ayako.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.340
You’re Sudou-san, right? I’ve heard a lot about you from my sis.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.050
Matsumoto talked about me?

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.680
Our villa is very close by.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.270
If it’s all right, I’d like to introduce you during dinner.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:57.900
Sudou-sempai!

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.870
Didn’t you say “for your ears only”?!

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:03.880
It was top secret! You liar! Repay me for that lunch!

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.380
Uhh, well, this is...

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.680
Tsunayoshi, you like beauties too? I see.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.130
That’s your dog, Sudou-sempai?

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:19.040
It does kinda resemble you...

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.970
Are you Kotoko-san by any chance?

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.540
How did you know about me?

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:27.230
Because, you’re exactly as my sis described.

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:29.680
What kind of description?

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.640
Irie-san is also exactly as my sis described.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.600
Being intelligent on top of having those looks. How wonderful.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.260
Maybe I should aim for him too.

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:40.570
What are you saying?!

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:45.600
A bear? Help!

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.610
It’s okay. This is our pension watchdog. He’s called Tiny.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.120
Cute, isn’t he?

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.860
Tiny? What’s tiny about him?

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.770
What a great welcome. Good for you.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:59.350
Wait, wait... Irie-kun!

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.120
So heavy...

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.320
Why did it turn out like this?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.600
Damn those Matsumoto sisters!

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:17.160
Because of those two, I can’t get close to Irie-kun at all!

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.870
What are you gonna do about this?!

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:19.980
Calm down.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:23.020
Spring break is gonna end!

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.990
Don’t worry. I have a special plan!

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.190
Plan?

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.020
Yeah, we’ll carry it out tomorrow.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:37.050
It’s a plan to bring true happiness to you and Irie, and me and Matsumoto.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:38.020
Listen up.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:47.300
If you memorize the name of the flower and its floriography...

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:51.870
...you might be able to knock him out with your femininity.

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:56.140
I see! All right! I’m gonna memorize these.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.330
First of all...

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:06.590
Kotoko!

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:14.250
Irie-kun!

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.230
You finally woke up.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:18.570
Would you like to take a stroll?

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:22.630
An opportunity has suddenly opened up?

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:25.510
What should I do?

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.370
That’s right! The floriography.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:33.580
What was this flower called again?

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:38.220
It’s always you telling me that you love me and such.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:42.430
But, do you know my true feelings?

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.810
You don’t feel anything for me, because it seems you never show your true feelings.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.310
Idiot.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.790
You’ve got it wrong, I...

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.700
I don’t believe it!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.960
The second time?!

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.700
Second...

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.870
A dream?

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:16.960
So it was a dream. That sure surprised me.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:19.500
I had a feeling it was too good to be true.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:29.650
But, strangely, there’s some kind of sensation left behind on my lips.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:45.330
To deepen our friendship, today...

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:49.080
...we’re going to have a couple orienteering event.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:53.290
To ensure safety, each pair will take a dog with them.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:56.240
Let’s decide the pairs immediately then.

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.170
Let’s use this lottery to decide fairly...

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.840
Hold it right there!

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.770
Don’t look at the folded part!

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:09.710
Everyone can trace along the lines however they like.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:10.770
Rejected!

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.440
After all we went through...

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.650
What did you go through?

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.370
Nevermind, it’s nothing.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:25.700
Let’s do it using a fairer and easier way.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:28.040
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.320
One, two... Rock, paper, scissors!

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.060
Rock, we’re rock!

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.800
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.540
First team: the rock pair.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:45.800
Matsumoto, best regards.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.830
Second team: the scissors pair.

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.460
Best regards, Irie-san.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.190
Ah, best regards.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.260
Third team: the paper pair.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.240
Don’t say I’m like paper as well!

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.200
Hey! What do you mean by “as well”?

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.120
Okay, so we’ll start five minutes apart.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:11.200
First up, top batters, Aihara and Little Brother Irie Team, go!

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.000
Okay...

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:17.870
Sheesh, why do I have to get Kotoko?

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.340
I’ve found you, Kotoko.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.600
There it is!

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.560
Yuuki-kun, the stamp.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.060
I know! Quit your nagging.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.070
You can be such a jerk.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:37.620
Hey, Tsunayoshi!

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:40.230
He probably got confused because you’re so fat.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:44.950
I won’t experience even a fragment of romance if this keeps up.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:47.820
I wonder what Irie-kun and Ayako-chan are doing right now...

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:51.550
What was that?

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:52.790
What’s wrong, Tiny?

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:02.310
Hey, what is it?

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:06.840
Huh... Bears?!

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.560
I thought I heard Kotoko’s voice.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.920
Thank goodness, it didn’t chase us.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.990
There’s nothing to be thankful about.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.210
Where are we?

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.990
It’s okay, Yuuki-kun. We’ll just go back the way we came.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:41.380
That was close.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.190
Dummy.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:52.850
There, there now, Clarice-chan. I wasn’t trying to do anything.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.740
Matsumoto, please do something.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:14:00.870
I can’t. Clarice has been trained to be merciless to suspicious people.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.820
Suspicious people?

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.660
That’s Kotoko’s hat!

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.620
I’m sure of it. Don’t tell me...

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.920
What a terrible predicament!

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:26.170
Kotoko, I’m coming to save you now!
Wait for me!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:31.590
All right!

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:44.240
Say, Irie-san. Would you like to walk some more? Just the two of us.

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:46.900
I have to prepare dinner.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:55.180
Kotoko!

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:01.730
Let’s head back.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.350
Wait!

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:12.250
Sudou-san, did you see Aihara or Yuuki on the way back?

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:14.510
They’re not back yet?

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.890
No, they aren’t.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.900
They were the first to leave, weren’t they?

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:23.400
Honestly, what are they doing? The sun is already going to set.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.150
It’s suddenly gotten much colder.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.590
And I’m hungry too.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:35.780
I think we really should look for a way back.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:40.360
I told you already! It’s dangerous to wander around randomly.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.630
Here.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.650
Why?

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.180
Yuuki-kun, you’re amazing!

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:59.780
How did the saying go again?

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:01.810
“Happiness comes to the prepared!”

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.810
“No distress comes to the prepared”, wasn’t it?

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.310
Yeah, that’s it!

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:10.540
Thank you. You’re very reliable, Yuuki-kun.

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:15.380
It’s because you’re too unreliable.
Even though you’re a college student.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:18.890
Ow, ow.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:22.160
I’m starving and I’m hurting everywhere.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.830
I’m a goner.

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:26.920
Kotoko, please hold on.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:31.990
Damn! I won’t be able to climb that high with this foot.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.840
At this rate, I’ll definitely...

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:39.380
No, I don’t want that!

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:42.230
Kotoko, I love you!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.240
Kotoko!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:48.380
What was that? A wolf?

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:51.370
There are no wolves in modern Japan, stupid!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:54.280
Then, what in the world is that?!

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.310
A stray dog, right?

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:58.390
Tsunayoshi, chase it away!

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:00.100
There’s only one.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.760
Tsunayoshi!

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.400
Tsunayoshi! What are you doing?!

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.100
That traitor dog!

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.570
Stand back, Kotoko.

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:27.600
Get lost, damn you!

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:33.780
Someone! Irie-kun!

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:38.450
Tiny!

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.450
Thank you!

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.540
Yuuki! Kotoko! Are you guys all right?

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.780
Irie-kun!

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.260
Yuuki, are you hurt?

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:48.640
I’m fine.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:50.920
That howl from earlier...

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.630
That voice...

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.010
Oh, you found Aihara and Yuuki.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:57.960
That’s great.

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:01.650
Sudou-san, please take these two back first.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:03.400
I’ll catch up with you soon.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.890
Irie-kun?

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:12.770
Someone! Is anyone there? Anyone!

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.440
A person?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.820
I’m saved! Hey!

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:18.820
Here, grab on!

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:21.280
That voice!

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.440
Don’t tell me... Irie!

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:24.540
Hurry it up!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:28.920
Mind your own business!
Who asked for your help?

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:32.250
Oh really? I didn’t need to help you.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.760
Come on, wait!

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.980
Oh yeah! Kotoko! Gotta save her!

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.780
Calm down. She’s safe.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.730
She went back to the lodge first.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:53.520
Really?

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:56.740
Thank God! Really, thank God!

00:18:57.310 --> 00:19:00.720
Sheesh. I concede defeat
to his pure-hearted love.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:06.160
Kotoko.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:09.400
Kin-chan? No, he’s not here.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.430
Eh, really?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.420
Okay, understood. Bye.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:16.960
From your father?

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.280
Yeah. He’s angry because Kin-chan has been absent from work.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:21.980
He said that he’ll fire him if he doesn’t show today.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:25.270
Oh no! Boss is really pissed!

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:27.210
I’ll be back soon.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:31.900
Oh, Irie-kun.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.440
Welcome back!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.560
Onii-chan, welcome back!

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:38.150
Tsunayoshi!

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:39.660
You traitor dog!

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:45.210
Thanks for letting us stay!

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:46.070
Bye bye.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:47.190
See you!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.100
Even though I went all the way to Romance Village...

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:56.370
...nothing romantic at all happened.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:06.010
But...

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.850
...I managed to kiss him in a dream though.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:12.850
Welcome back everyone.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.600
We’re back!

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:17.460
So, how did things at Romance Village go?

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.490
Were you able to make some
lovely memories?

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:24.070
Well, how should I put it...?

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.370
Ah, Papa, welcome back.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.870
Naoki, come. We have to talk.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:37.880
I got a call from your university today.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:42.380
Is it true that you’re transferring to the Medical Department?

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:45.600
Yes. I’m transferring this April.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:48.220
What? I never heard about this!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.220
I’m sorry for keeping this from you.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:53.230
It’s just that I’ve been thinking...

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:57.440
...about what I really want to do, and whether I really have no dreams.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:02.070
Naoki, I want you to be my successor.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.120
I’m going to become a doctor.

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:07.410
I’m not going to succeed your company. I’ve already made up my mind.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:09.470
Naoki!

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:16.170
Dad!

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.700
Dad! What’s wrong?

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:20.670
My chest...

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:21.590
Papa!

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:23.960
What’s wrong? Hang in there!

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:25.130
Papa!

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:27.300
Kotoko! The ambulance!

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:28.710
Right!

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:10.230
Irie-kun is having a marriage interview?!

00:23:10.230 --> 00:23:11.950
So, what do you plan to do, Aihara-san?

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:14.080
I don’t know. And you, Matsumoto-san?

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:16.200
I’m going to oppose, obviously!

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:18.770
As I thought. This is one of the rare occasions we get along.

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:20.540
By the way, who’s the girl he’s meeting?

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:22.880
Surely someone who’s no competition...

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:26.150
What’s going on? So dazzling!

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:28.260
Next time on Itazura na Kiss:

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:29.570
Mismatched hearts.

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:32.750
I’m definitely gonna be happy... aren’t I?
